DArc's changes to GRZipII/libGRZip (Grebnov Ilya, 2002-2004):

1. Added an early check in LZP_Encode
2. Removed CRC computation/checking
3. Changed the encoding of Mode to widen the range of MinMatchLen/HashSize in LZP

These describe the vendored C, which no longer lives here: the codec is
rust/darc-codecs/src/grzip/ and all three changes are carried into it. The list
is kept because it is the only record of how DArc's GRZip stream differs from
stock libGRZip -- the two are not interchangeable, so anyone comparing the port
against an upstream libGRZip needs to know which one it is meant to match.

The C is still reachable at the revision rust/difftest/c-reference.sh pins,
which is where grzip-check.sh builds its oracle from.
